      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "route_only"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The pueblo is a member of the Eight Northern Pueblos and its people speak the Rio Grande Tewa language.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Clara_Pueblo%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Santa Clara is renowned for hand‑crafted blackware and redware pottery, often featuring incised “knife‑wing” or eagle feather designs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12,
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Clara_Pueblo%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Puye Cliff Dwellings park, a National Historic Landmark, showcases ancestral villages and cliff dwellings managed by Santa Clara Pueblo.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Clara_Pueblo%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A Spanish chapel built in 1617 was replaced by a new church in 1918, reflecting the pueblo’s long colonial history.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Santa_Clara_Pueblo%2C_New_Mexico",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Archaeological evidence shows Ancestral Puebloans inhabited the region as far back as 1200 BC, long before Spanish arrival in 1598.",
